<script>
  import reports from '#lib/data/reports-4471.json';
  import notes from '#lib/data/desk-notes.json';
  import { groupByCause, readAs, uniqueById } from '#lib/kb/causes';
  import { tenantOf } from '#lib/kb/locales';
  import CauseTable from '#lib/kb/CauseTable.svelte';
  import Callout from '#lib/kb/Callout.svelte';
  import RenderStamp from '#lib/kb/RenderStamp.svelte';

  const repo = 'https://github.com/aniket-kulkarni/mega-s01e03-4471/issues';

  // The desk's own view of #4471, split one step further: the one-day moves it footnotes
  // (desk-notes.json) leave the cause they are filed under and get a ticket of their own.
  const merged = uniqueById(reports).filter((r) => r.mergedInto === 4471);
  const groups = groupByCause(merged, tenantOf);
  const count = (cause) => groups.find((g) => g.cause === cause)?.reports.length ?? 0;
  const moved = groups.reduce((n, g) => n + readAs(g, notes.oneDayMove), 0);
  const split = [
    { cause: 'parser', what: 'shared parser reads dates month first', n: count('parser') - moved, href: `${repo}/1` },
    { cause: 'hint', what: 'booking-v3 hints MM/DD/YYYY, reads DD/MM', n: count('hint'), href: `${repo}/2` },
    { cause: 'one-day move', what: 'dates move by one day across time zones', n: moved, href: `${repo}/3` },
  ];
</script>

[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked **known: one issue, one fix queued**. The reports in it
describe three different bugs. The queued parser fix closes only the first one. Each bug now has a
ticket of its own, and the counts below come from the merged reports at render time.

<Callout kind="warn">
Do not close #4471 when the parser fix ships. The booking-v3 form and the one-day moves will keep
coming in, and both need their own fixes.
</Callout>

## The split

<table>
  <thead><tr><th>bug</th><th>reports</th><th>ticket</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    {#each split as t (t.cause)}
      <tr><td><code>{t.cause}</code> · {t.what}</td><td>{t.n}</td><td><a href={t.href}>{t.href.replace('https://github.com/', '')}</a></td></tr>
    {/each}
    <tr><td>in #4471</td><td>{merged.length}</td><td></td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

## What #4471 holds, as the desk's table counts it

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The table files the one-day moves under the cause of their tenant and footnotes them. They are not a
parser swap, so the split above takes them out of `parser` and gives them their own ticket.

## The three bugs

- **`parser`: the shared parser reads dates month first** ([ticket](https://github.com/aniket-kulkarni/mega-s01e03-4471/issues/1)). Our tenants
  write the day first, so day and month swap. It covers app and email reports from every tenant, and
  form reports from booking-v2 tenants, whose hint already says `DD/MM/YYYY`.
- **`hint`: booking-v3 asks for month first and reads day first** ([ticket](https://github.com/aniket-kulkarni/mega-s01e03-4471/issues/2)). The form
  prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type what it says, and the form reads the
  tenant's way. These are form reports from booking-v3 tenants only. The parser fix does not touch
  them.
- **one-day move: the date moves by one day** ([ticket](https://github.com/aniket-kulkarni/mega-s01e03-4471/issues/3)). Day and month are not swapped.
  Lisbon gets Tuesday and Toronto gets Monday, "only June" is off, and an invite arrives before the
  booking. That is a time-zone or daylight-saving bug. The desk already noted these reports as a
  one-day move (`desk-notes.json`), but the cause table still files them under `parser` by tenant.

## How the split was made

- One id, one report: the export pages overlap, so repeated rows are dropped first.
- The cause comes from the tenant (its locale and booking form, `locales.ts`), never from intake's tag.
  Intake guesses from the reporter's browser. The `tagged as` column shows how often that guess is
  wrong.
- A report the desk read as a one-day move belongs to the time-zone ticket, whatever its tenant.

## For the desk

- Triage by subject ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) merged all three bugs
  because the reports share subject lines. Before you merge into a big ticket, check the cause with
  the [dedupe explorer](/kb/triage/dedupe).
- New date reports: file `hint` under the booking-v3 ticket, one-day moves under the time-zone ticket, and
  the rest under #4471.

